      "subtitle": "Pronombres interrogativos: what, where, when, who…",
      "goals": [
        "Elegir la palabra interrogativa correcta.",
        "Distinguir **how much** y **how many**.",
        "Ordenar preguntas: **wh- + verbo auxiliar + sujeto**."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Las palabras para preguntar",
      "table": {
        "head": ["Palabra", "Pregunta por…", "Ejemplo"],
        "rows": [
          ["**What**", "cosas, información", "What's your name?"],
          ["**Where**", "lugar", "Where do you live?"],
          ["**When**", "momento", "When is your birthday?"],
          ["**What time**", "la hora exacta", "What time is it?"],
          ["**Who**", "personas", "Who is your teacher?"],
          ["**Why**", "razón (respuesta con *because*)", "Why are you tired?"],
          ["**Which**", "elección entre opciones", "Which color do you prefer, red or blue?"],
          ["**How**", "modo, estado", "How are you? How do you get to school?"],
          ["**How old**", "edad", "How old are you?"],
          ["**How many**", "cantidad contable", "How many brothers have you got?"],
          ["**How much**", "cantidad incontable, precio", "How much water? How much is it?"]
        ],
        "speak": 2
      },
      "tip": "Orden: **Wh- + am/is/are + sujeto** (*Where **are you** from?*) o **Wh- + do/does + sujeto + verbo** (*Where **do you live**?*)."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
